WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.460
OT detection engineering turns telemetry and process knowledge into useful defensive signals.

2
00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:22.360
It is a lifecycle discipline: define a meaningful use case, understand the environment and evidence, write logic, validate safely, deploy with ownership, tune from results, maintain through change, and retire detections that no longer serve their purpose.

3
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:31.520
Effective detections depend on accurate asset identity, architecture, communication paths, protocol behavior, and process context.

4
00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:43.780
Network, endpoint, historian, identity, remote-access, firewall, and controller records each contribute part of the picture, with documented limitations and blind spots.

5
00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:50.620
Baselines describe expected devices, roles, timing, commands, and operating modes.

6
00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:55.120
Anomalies reveal change but do not prove malicious activity.

7
00:00:55.220 --> 00:01:06.740
Maintenance, equipment faults, and authorized engineering can look unusual, so operator and engineering collaboration is essential to reduce false positives and interpret consequence.

8
00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:09.980
Validation must protect safety and reliability.

9
00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:19.840
Use isolated tests, record review, tabletop analysis, engineering review, and passive production observation before considering any active method.

10
00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:26.340
Tune detections for evidence quality, investigation value, and safe action rather than maximum alert volume.

11
00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:33.260
A mature program documents ownership, versions, metrics, coverage, runbooks, and retirement.

12
00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:39.200
Its goal is trustworthy, actionable visibility that supports safe and reliable operations.

13
00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:42.020
More alerts are not the product.

14
00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:47.800
Better decisions, made with defensible evidence and operational collaboration, are.
